["diff --git a/docs/content/Release-Notes/0-31.mdx b/docs/content/Release-Notes/0-31.mdx
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..94d3931
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/content/Release-Notes/0-31.mdx
@@ -0,0 +1,123 @@
+---
+title: v0.31
+permalink: /releases/v0-31
+category: Release Notes
+---
+
+Hi Cube Community 👋 We're really excited to announce Cube v0.31 🎉 This new
+release brings a number of major new features such as:
+
+- Support for YAML modeling
+- Support for ksqlDB
+- Lambda pre-aggregations
+- Views
+
+## Breaking Changes and Deprecations
+
+Two breaking changes this release and 1 deprecation this release
+
+- **BREAKING CHANGE**: Foreign cube references must now reference a cube member
+- **BREAKING CHANGE**: The `shown` property now hides cubes/views from the
+  `/meta` endpoint when set to `true`
+- **DEPRECATION**: The `driverFactory` property should return a `DriverConfig`
+  object or a Promise that returns a `DriverConfig` object
+
+> Be sure to check the
+> [Deprecation document](https://github.com/cube-js/cube.js/blob/master/DEPRECATION.md)
+> for more details on the above.
+
+## Multiple Data Sources
+
+Cube has had support for multiple data sources for quite some time now, but
+we’ve made it even easier to configure them now with environment variables.
+[Read the documentation](https://cube.dev/docs/config/multiple-data-sources) to
+see how it works.
+
+## Modeling in YAML
+
+We’ve often heard users they want the ability to author data models in languages
+other than JavaScript - specifically YAML and Python. Today, we’re excited to
+release a public preview for YAML data modeling in Cube. Check out the
+[introductory blog post](https://cube.dev/blog/introducing-cube-support-for-yaml-data-modeling),
+or dive straight into
+[the documentation](https://cube.dev/docs/schema/getting-started/yaml).
+
+## Views
+
+Designed as a layer over cubes, views act as a façade of your whole data model.
+They are a great tool for to defining metrics, managing governance and data
+access, and controlling ambiguous join paths. Learn more about them in the
+[introductory blog post](https://cube.dev/blog/introducing-views), read more
+about them [in the documentation](https://cube.dev/docs/schema/reference/view)
+or watch our in-depth
+[webinar on the topic](https://cube.dev/events/using-cube-views-for-metrics-management).
+
+## Lambda Pre-Aggregations
+
+Lambda pre-aggregations allow combining batched/processed data with fresh data
+at query time, this is super useful for real-time data applications. You can
+even take it a step further and combine batched data from a data warehouse with
+streaming data from ksqlDB; find more information
+[in the documentation](https://cube.dev/docs/caching/pre-aggregations/lambda-pre-aggregations).
+
+## Drivers
+
+We’re really excited to present two new drivers,
+[Firebolt](https://cube.dev/docs/config/databases/firebolt) and Trino. And to
+top it off, we’ve also added a brand-new driver for
+[ksqlDB](https://cube.dev/docs/config/databases/ksqldb).
+
+## SQL API
+
+The Cube SQL API now speaks the Postgres protocol instead of MySQL; the Postgres
+protocol is better supported and allows us to extend supports to dozens of
+downstream tools. We’ve also made a number of improvements relating syntax and
+operator support, and we’ve documented
+[any difference in behaviour](https://cube.dev/docs/backend/sql/reference/functions-operators)
+from regular SQL.
+
+## Downstream Tools
+
+We’ve been busy since the last release adding support for downstream tools. Cube
+now connects to:
+
+- [Appsmith](https://cube.dev/docs/config/downstream/appsmith)
+- [Tableau](https://cube.dev/docs/config/downstream/tableau/)
+- [Microsoft PowerBI](https://cube.dev/docs/config/downstream/powerbi/)
+- Thoughtspot
+- Amazon QuickSight
+
+Let us know if there’s a tool that you’d like supported by opening an issue on
+GitHub.
+
+## Community Contributions
+
+As always, we have a long list of contributions from the community this release,
+and we'd like to thank each and every person who took the time to help us
+improve Cube 😁
+
+- [@hashman](https://github.com/hashman)
+- [@magno32](https://github.com/magno32)
+- [@joacoc](https://github.com/joacoc)
+- [@olejeglejeg](https://github.com/olejeglejeg)
+- [@reify-thomas-smith](https://github.com/reify-thomas-smith)
+- [@Jeseeq](https://github.com/Jeseeq)
+- [@alexbarrett](https://github.com/alexbarrett)
+- [@puzpuzpuz](https://github.com/puzpuzpuz)
